 "notes": "Headline result: dark photon DM (DPDM) resonant conversion in solar corona observed with LOFAR (30-80 MHz). 95% C.L. upper limit on kinetic mixing epsilon, Fig.4 (plots/limits.pdf), cyan LOFAR region lower boundary traced from vector stroke (drawing idx5). Y-axis is eps*(rho_A/rho_DM)^0.5; for the papers own limit rho_A=rho_DM=0.3 GeV/cm^3 so the factor is 1 and the curve equals epsilon directly. X-axis m_A in 10^-7 eV (log), calibrated on major ticks (m=1..6 at x=99..792.5); Y log calibrated on decade ticks 10^-10..10^-14 at y=65..481.1. Mass range 1.25e-7 to 3.28e-7 eV (f=30-80 MHz, E=h*f). Spiky observed limit ~3e-14 to 1.4e-12, ~1e-13 typical. Axion-photon case also derived but paper states it is weaker than existing bounds and not the main result.",
